One of the biggest differences not mentioned above: In Crawl, you
cannot sell objects. Your only source of $ is picking up gold on the
floor or dropped by monsters, and your only use of $ is to buy stuff
you see in shops. This nicely diverts about 75% of your attention
from "what objects do I have in my pack / bag / stash" to "what
skills do I have", which seems to be one of the main goals of the
crawl effort.

One convenience in Crawl is autoexplore (or whatever it's called).
Press a key, and your character starts automatically exploring the
entire level. And you can configure what's "interesting" that stops
the autoexplore: stop when you see an object, or automatically pick
it up; stop when you see a monster, or ignore it; etc.  This feature
was really neat at first ... then it made the whole game start to
seem like a TV show instead of a game to me. So I stopped playing
crawl for a while.


